# Data pipeline

- Treat raw inputs as immutable and verify their checksums before processing.
- Make each cleaning, alignment, thresholding, and final-filter stage explicit.
- Record rows, sessions, animals, columns, checksum, producer, and source
  artifact for every stage.
- Validate required columns, uniqueness assumptions, category values, and
  animal membership at load boundaries.
- Restrict committed processed data to publication inputs and figure summaries.
- Keep side analyses out of `data/processed/`.
- Use Parquet for typed trial-level data and JSON for manifests.
- Never silently drop rows. Every filtering stage must report its counts.
- Resolve paths through `violations_glm.paths` and allow
  `VIOLATIONS_GLM_DATA_DIR` for external Zenodo data.
